"""A small web page for trying this solution on your own computer.

    python app.py            # then open http://127.0.0.1:8000
    python app.py --port 8080

The page (``ui/index.html``) takes the solution's inputs, starts ``run_poc.py`` and shows
what it wrote. Another front end can call the same server:

    GET  /api/solution                    what the solution is, takes in and gives out
    POST /api/run                         multipart form: ``files`` (any number), and the
                                          optional text fields ``question`` and ``text``
    GET  /api/status                      whether a run is going, and the end of its log
    GET  /api/runs/<id>/files/<name>      one output file of a run
    GET  /api/source                      this package's source code as a zip

``POST /api/run`` answers with JSON: ``ok``, ``exit_code``, ``log_tail``, ``outputs``
(``name``, ``kind``, ``size``, ``url``), ``result`` (the main JSON output, when there is
one) and ``source_trace`` (the source check's report, when the solution writes one).
A refusal is ``{"ok": false, "error": {"code": ..., "message": ...}}``.

Every run gets a working folder of its own in the system's temporary folder: the
package's code, the files sent with the request in ``sample_input/`` and an empty
``output/``. The package's own ``sample_input/`` and ``output/`` are never written to.
A request that sends no file runs on the examples in the package's ``sample_input/``.

``GET /api/source`` zips what the package is made of, and only that: its Python files
(this server among them), ``README.md``, ``config.yaml``, ``requirements.txt``,
``.env.example`` (unless it gives a key a value) and ``.gitignore``, the text files in
``schemas/`` and ``prompts/``, and this page's own files in ``ui/``. Nothing else goes
in: no other hidden file (``.env`` and its keys among them), no file whose name says it
holds a credential, nothing from ``sample_input/``, ``output/`` or ``evals/ground_truth/``
whatever the case of their names, no virtual environment, run folder or link. It is off
while the server listens on the network.

There is no sign-in. The server listens on this computer only (127.0.0.1) unless you
start it with ``--host``; do that only on a network you trust. Ctrl+C, SIGTERM and
SIGHUP (the terminal closing) stop a run that is going and remove the working folders.
Standard library only. Run as ``python app.py``, the package's folder heads ``sys.path``;
the server takes it out before its other imports, so a file there named like a library
module is not imported in the library's place.
"""

# The other imports wait until sys.path is cleaned.
# ruff: noqa: E402
import os
import sys

if __name__ == "__main__":
    # A secrets.py or ipaddress.py next to this file would otherwise be imported
    # in place of the standard library's and change what this unchanged server
    # does. It needs no module of the package's: run_poc.py runs as a process of
    # its own. os and sys are loaded before this file is.
    _HERE = os.path.normcase(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    sys.path[:] = [
        p for p in sys.path if os.path.normcase(os.path.realpath(p or os.curdir)) != _HERE
    ]

